  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_f7dfc730ce4c458a8dd8ca099e79bf6b",
      "statement": "Static equity portfolio selection distinguishes three mixed-integer constraint families: minimum trading lots (assets traded only in integer numbers of lots), a maximum number of distinct holdings, and a minimum number of lots that must be bought if a stock is selected.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/06_constraints_and_metaheuristics.md#L16-L20",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f897a7236cb50be9e302e1cc1ccbcd6f96e69816effbaada39c4e9f53c099c86:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_133ae9fa8bbc4f368914e3120beb181e",
      "statement": "Introducing mixed-integer constraints makes checking feasibility of the constraint system in general NP-complete and solving the problem in general NP-hard, where NP-hard is at least as hard as NP-complete and NP-complete problems admit no polynomial-time solution algorithm.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/06_constraints_and_metaheuristics.md#L22-L27",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:813d24e751a3efec2ed8fe8c8d8fb707c1df56626d6d4f22f7d8d6458d1f51d0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_87ef2cf0e8ce462c984433cbdddc0433",
      "statement": "For the system Ax≤b, #{i:x_i>0}≤K, 0≤x_i≤u_i with a single cardinality constraint, verifying feasibility is NP-complete already when M≥3 (three linear inequality rows), so the difficulty comes from the joint cardinality-plus-few-inequalities structure, not from the portfolio dimension N.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/06_constraints_and_metaheuristics.md#L31-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d970d96a5c1bce66f8316dcce753511045c2ed4c6769cbf12bfa211d14172d84:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ea7d211cd66d4507aa0b9889c4785f99",
      "statement": "In the minimum-lot Andramonov-Corazza model the objective (PLx)'V(PLx) rewrites as the quadratic form x'(L'P'VPL)x, and a two-stage branch-and-bound / cutting-plane / sub-gradient scheme has a termination guarantee: if at least one asset is infinitely divisible it either finds the optimum or reports the feasible region empty in finitely many iterations.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/06_constraints_and_metaheuristics.md#L55-L78",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a996b144af6ba85d9fabfc3344d2c214a4a31f86b8ad092c3a2cf354dd01f814:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fbcab149355142509f9fff53c5cb726a",
      "statement": "The Corazza-Favaretto integer-lot model has a feasible solution if and only if r_1≥π (the reference asset meets the required return), or else r_1<π and there exists a stock ī in I={2,...,N+1} with r_ī>r_1 dominating the reference asset in mean return.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/06_constraints_and_metaheuristics.md#L106-L128",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c5b701c424ec94629efeedc0042591e94d9a5e699c15a030b3113dfe5a0b2af3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_af4451a8bf0249fdab33b55bec36d276",
      "statement": "The Jansen-Van Dijk index-tracking model minimizes tracking error volatility TEV(x)=Var(r_portfolio−r_benchmark) subject to x'e=1, an exact cardinality #{i:x_i>0}=K and x≥0, and is approximated by moving cardinality into the objective (weighted by c≥0) using #{i:x_i>0}=lim_{p↓0}(x_1^p,...,x_N^p)'e with a small p.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/06_constraints_and_metaheuristics.md#L136-L180",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f6bddff61adf04a1ce87d9694927cf79f82d778f8583c9980a724b1a9edf802e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_22ce51b5ad0d4df8bfba1bdaadce19eb",
      "statement": "Cardinality constraints can make the efficient frontier discontinuous: on an N=4, K=2 example the mean-variance frontier is two separate, unconnected arcs, exemplifying that integer constraints destroy analytic properties the classical continuous frontier possesses.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/06_constraints_and_metaheuristics.md#L182-L184",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2dae1c9962fdf37dc0baf4fdb0d02e1f887ea8e904964d00e3ec99fe3fa7a55c:"
        }
