        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_077d2f29520248609b1a9849d67f94bb",
      "statement": "Semi-variance is a downside-risk measure summing only below-benchmark deviations Σ_{t:r_t<r̄}(r_t−r̄)²/T; it equals variance for symmetric returns but is not analytically tractable.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/06_constraints_and_metaheuristics.md#L216-L222",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7760c52927d148d7b1fc4b1b7017c8ded9530fcca9ea67c307168e62a927a359:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d0010b979b75430381d18d896e5c8332",
      "statement": "Mean absolute deviation MAD(r)=Σ_t|r_t−r̄|/T is outlier-sensitive but less so than variance; because of the absolute value its optimization problem is linear whereas the variance problem is quadratic.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/06_constraints_and_metaheuristics.md#L224-L230",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:160e1565cb891884bd361aff05d1c493ac9378ddaf9fb9c4a7bb565de7530bd5:"
