    {
      "id": "claim_dfc54756e6b248c6b8a38e1e59a5a0e3",
      "statement": "The mixed-integer mean-variance model minimizes λΣ x_i x_j σ_ij − (1−λ)Σ x_i μ_i subject to x'e=1, Σz_i=K, ε_i z_i≤x_i≤δ_i z_i, z_i∈{0,1}, with λ=0 maximizing return, λ=1 minimizing risk, and intermediate λ a trade-off; swapping the risk term yields mean-semi-variance and MAD models and adding the third moment yields mean-variance-skewness.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/06_constraints_and_metaheuristics.md#L244-L261",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bab044e064e3b0946bc2b4afb399f6ab2b1910e5253856f9ec4ebd374649702e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b20e37f2aa2843a78b874aed5fb86c7e",
      "statement": "The physical-quantity (x_i) and wealth-proportion (w_i) formulations of the constrained model describe exactly the same feasible set, and the w_i form is the one used in the mixed-integer models.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/06_constraints_and_metaheuristics.md#L263-L277",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f4f497e0da9eb9c235e5a75c79dcede7c896c568740e9d70c1919234232c249d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_484b9a34a9b24ec89200e4d463cfa210",
      "statement": "Metaheuristics are an iterative generation process guiding a subordinate heuristic that balances exploration (visiting diverse regions) against exploitation (refining a promising area); they are problem-agnostic, approximate, stochastic, can escape local minima, may use memory, and are classified as population- vs trajectory-based and by inspiration (evolutionary, physics-based, human-based, swarm-based).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/06_constraints_and_metaheuristics.md#L279-L281",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f181a9742872ba364b43c5b00e3ae872108b2b93c6f76703eb657e1201a67c48:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2d9936204620449faea84aff78bc859b",
      "statement": "The Exact Penalty Method rewrites min f(x) with equality and inequality constraints as min f(x)+(1/ε)[Σ|g_r(x)−a_r|+Σ max(0,b_s−h_s(x))], and is 'exact' because a finite threshold of ε (rather than ε→0) makes the constrained and unconstrained optima coincide.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/06_constraints_and_metaheuristics.md#L283-L297",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fd644fa9d8669893448127507960c983d4b05bcedc2d38259660461344adb2ff:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_eff46c957f5747cb9f7e54dabedaef4b",
      "statement": "The binary constraint z_i∈{0,1} is enforced by the ad-hoc violation term z_i(1−z_i), which is zero exactly on {0,1} and positive for any other real value, letting the whole mixed-integer mean-variance model be reformulated as a single unconstrained penalty-weighted objective.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/06_constraints_and_metaheuristics.md#L299-L324",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:83d885e7204ab9bd598719eea3f26967fcf7b1a48d7a917653788de17bc38854:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9d93bf22345f4e22b49c98fe76691f40",
      "statement": "Particle Swarm Optimization is a nature-inspired, iterative, population-based, memory-using, derivative-free metaheuristic for unconstrained global optimization that mimics foraging birds, each particle a candidate solution randomly placed in the feasible set with a random initial velocity.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/06_constraints_and_metaheuristics.md#L328-L330",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:db53e6ada9be1095822ae5df1f9136b4a5fa19079616299e54b285c99ae62eee:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_df4300ad74094718933dcdcab0125584",
      "statement": "In PSO the velocity update v_j^{k+1}=w^{k+1}v_j^k + U_{φ1}⊗(p_j−x_j^k) + U_{φ2}⊗(p_g−x_j^k) combines an inertia term, a cognitive term toward the personal best, and a social term toward the global best, with the neighborhood best determined by the topology (fully connected, von Neumann, or ring).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/06_constraints_and_metaheuristics.md#L340-L353",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d15e0d55f5c4e573329db295cbedcaa060f1eff4a5eb8672fb791a21cf42a040:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_55eae694658c4d99a7ab73cb8c9dcb47",
      "statement": "The inertia weight is typically linearly decreasing w^k = w_max + ((w_min−w_max)/K)k with w_min=0.4 and w_max=0.9, or constant w=0.7298 in which case a velocity cap prevents divergence.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/06_constraints_and_metaheuristics.md#L355-L361",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1207252ccf23716164dd58829157df57f3488d55395e1bbf4b9cb666924ec0cc:"
