      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e91ea0cded7247fc84d1e5d8865aa196",
      "statement": "Standard PSO reaches the global optimum in probability — a probabilistic guarantee consistent with the stochastic nature of metaheuristics, not deterministic finite-step convergence.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/06_constraints_and_metaheuristics.md#L363-L365",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fc84a78c41d6de660a4d80672918e99f73e5e0660f73d2c41f31001e3941985d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c193003e5798462e847bf36ee321283d",
      "statement": "On the base D=3 mean-variance problem reformulated as min x'Vx + (1/ε)(|x'r−π|+|x'e−1|), ε=0.0001 is too small to balance variance against constraints while ε=0.001 concentrates the PSO cloud around the Markowitz optimum, and more particles (N=30) improve both speed and quality of convergence.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/06_constraints_and_metaheuristics.md#L377-L391",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9217f000faab620baf9aa0a92eb7f0c5837fe6b91742c1c2d3004b7dec178cd7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f32b8171241a44dea3e67828b46ab650",
      "statement": "With N=30 and normalized random initialization the budget constraint x'e=1 holds exactly in 100% of simulations while the equality return constraint holds between 0% and 90% across scenarios, and relaxing the return constraint to an inequality x'R≥R_P concentrates the PSO points even more tightly since a particle may exceed the required return without penalty.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/06_constraints_and_metaheuristics.md#L393-L399",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:db153d855e50791325b1f45c25657a465f0240e3a97808920fc92da3551e967d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e763dcd53dfb46e59c80136cdd2c579b",
      "statement": "On the FTSE-MIB mixed-integer mean-variance experiment (40 particles, 4000 iterations, penalty 0.0001, w=0.7298, c_1=c_2=1.49618, ε_i=1%, δ_i=50%, λ=0.5), exactly K assets get z_i≈1 and x_i>0 with the objective value 15.2432 at K=10 versus 11.5738 at K=20, convergence stabilizing near zero after about 1200–1500 iterations, and the K=10 portfolio reaching about 1.47 out-of-sample (Jan–Jun 2009) from a unit base.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/06_constraints_and_metaheuristics.md#L401-L414",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b3252f05037343727e7e3c817f7324739b48aab8e6a042c0fbb7f0ed004d7f8b:"
        }
      ]
    }
